    "anatomical_requirements": "# Anatomical Requirements\n\nRender anatomically correct characters.\n\n- Every visible hand has exactly five fingers in the correct anatomical arrangement.\n- Hands, wrists, elbows, shoulders, legs, feet, necks, and torsos are naturally connected.\n- No extra limbs, missing limbs, fused limbs, duplicated body parts, or disconnected anatomy.\n- Fingers have natural proportions and believable poses.\n- Character interactions do not cause anatomy to intersect or merge.",
    "avoid": "# Avoid\n\n- Inconsistent character identity.\n- Wrong costume.\n- Modern objects.\n- Unreadable faces.\n- Merged characters.\n- Cropped characters.\n- Anatomical distortions.",
    "high_risk_elements": "# High-Risk Elements\n\nPay particular attention to:\n\n- Hands making gestures.\n- Characters sitting with crossed legs.\n- Characters touching or closely facing each other.\n- Objects held in the hands.\n- Long ears remaining fully attached and correctly shaped.\n- Hair remaining consistent with the reference.",
    "final_verification": "# Final Verification\n\n<!-- ZET:BEGIN IMAGE_PROMPT_ONLY -->\nBefore producing the final image, verify that:\n<!-- ZET:END IMAGE_PROMPT_ONLY -->\n<!-- ZET:BEGIN ANALYSIS_PROMPT_ONLY -->\nCheck the candidate image for these visible requirements:\n<!-- ZET:END ANALYSIS_PROMPT_ONLY -->\n\n- Character count and identities exactly match the scene description.\n- Every character is in the correct left/right position and depth.\n- Every visible hand has exactly five fingers with correct anatomy.\n- Arms, legs, feet, ears, and clothing are fully connected and anatomically correct.\n- Characters are completely separate; no merged bodies or intersecting limbs.\n- Props are held naturally and are clearly readable.\n- Eye lines and interactions match the story beat.\n- Costumes and recurring character features match the supplied references.\n- The setting, lighting, mood, and art style match the scene specification."
